1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,580
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,930
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:06,030
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:08,920
I've laid carpet for
forty-one years.

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,030
Forty-one years on my
knees,

6
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:12,590
crawling room to room,

7
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:13,490
hitting a knee kicker

8
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,630
with my right knee

9
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:16,350
a few hundred times a day.

10
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:17,900
Two years ago that knee

11
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,360
finally got replaced.

12
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,280
It has hurt every day
since.

13
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:22,940
Not surgery pain.

14
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:24,690
I know what that felt
like,

15
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:25,700
and it went away.

16
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:26,740
This is different.

17
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,370
Tight.

18
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:28,130
Full.

19
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:29,100
Like a band around

20
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,600
the joint that never
loosens.

21
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:31,740
And for two years I've

22
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:32,990
been told the same thing.

23
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,150
Give it time.

24
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:35,840
At six weeks it was
swelling,

25
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,130
and swelling is normal.

26
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,010
At three months,

27
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:39,060
give it six.

28
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:40,020
At six months,

29
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,640
some knees take a full
year.

30
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:42,540
At a year,

31
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,310
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

32
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:45,780
And I didn't just wait.

33
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,070
We went down the list.

34
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:48,430
More physical therapy.

35
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,440
Every session,

36
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,910
every exercise at home.

37
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,130
I got stronger.

38
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,030
The tightness never moved.

39
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,640
The pain pills helped,

40
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,050
and that was the problem.

41
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:59,560
I'm already on enough
every morning,

42
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,610
and nobody could tell me

43
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:01,860
when I'd get to stop.

44
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:02,870
Then a nerve block.

45
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:04,810
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

46
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:06,230
And after that, a second

47
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:07,300
operation to go back

48
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,390
in and do it over.

49
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:09,920
I said no.

50
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:11,620
On the job I tried

51
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:13,590
everything a carpet man
tries.

52
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,380
Gel kneepads, then thicker
kneepads.

53
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,590
The power stretcher
instead of the kicker,

54
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:20,140
even in the little
bedrooms.

55
00:01:20,290 --> 00:01:22,230
Letting the young guy on
my crew

56
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:23,290
do the kicking

57
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:24,800
while I cut the seams.

58
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:26,070
Every morning

59
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:27,810
I climbed down out of the
truck

60
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:28,920
and my knee felt like

61
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,670
a band was wrapped around
it,

62
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:32,890
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

63
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,340
Every morning

64
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:35,030
I took something

65
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:36,740
for it and went to work.

66
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:38,970
Couldn't carry a roll up
the stairs,

67
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:40,230
couldn't stay down long
enough

68
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:41,660
to finish a closet,

69
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,480
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

70
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,600
without shifting every two
minutes.

71
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:47,100
It woke me at night,

72
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,030
and it turned ordinary
things,

73
00:01:49,030 --> 00:01:50,410
like getting in the truck

74
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:51,910
or up off the floor,

75
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:53,060
into a decision.

76
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:54,590
Getting down on that
carpet

77
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:56,000
was never the hard part.

78
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:58,170
Getting back up was the
part

79
00:01:58,170 --> 00:01:59,730
I started planning for.

80
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,260
And I started doing the
math

81
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,390
on how many more years

82
00:02:02,390 --> 00:02:03,360
I had in me.

83
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:06,030
Because a carpet man who
can't kneel

84
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,290
isn't a carpet man.

85
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,250
After a long and serious

86
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:10,460
talk with my wife,

87
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:12,460
I went back in one more
time.

88
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:13,740
That was the fourth set

89
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,700
of X-rays on this knee.

90
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,780
And like the three before
it,

91
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:20,090
the answer was everything
looks great.

92
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:22,110
No loosening, no
infection,

93
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:23,050
nothing wrong.

94
00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:24,360
Only this time

95
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,730
there was no new number.

96
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:28,020
Nobody said give it
another six months.

97
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,550
There was nothing left to
give it.

98
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:30,740
I sat in the parking

99
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:31,700
lot for a while.

100
00:02:32,050 --> 00:02:32,930
Okay, I thought.

101
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:34,030
Then explain this.

102
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,990
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

103
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:37,410
I hit my breaking point.

104
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:39,320
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

105
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:41,540
Everyone in the house was
asleep

106
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:43,250
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

107
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:44,400
with my leg up,

108
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,020
trying to find any angle
where

109
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:47,190
it didn't feel like
something

110
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:48,700
was wrapped around my knee

111
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:49,600
and tightening.

112
00:02:49,830 --> 00:02:51,540
I had a job booked at
seven.

113
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:53,270
A whole upstairs,

114
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:54,900
three bedrooms and a
hallway.

115
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,500
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

116
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,350
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

117
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,600
And I just thought,

118
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,260
is this really my life
now?

119
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:03,820
I can't live like this.

120
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,740
So I made myself a
promise.

121
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:06,760
I wouldn't go a day

122
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,270
without looking for an
answer.

123
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,000
And when I found one,

124
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,280
I'd share it with everyone

125
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:12,610
going through the same
thing.

126
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,030
So I got my laptop

127
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:15,530
out and went looking.

128
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:17,270
Not for a product.

129
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:18,730
For an explanation.

130
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:20,480
Mayo Clinic forums,

131
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,930
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

132
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:25,780
doctor videos, medical
animations.

133
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:27,270
And that's when I found a
video

134
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:29,170
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

135
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:30,670
Steven Salinger,

136
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:31,880
whose own wife had been

137
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,380
through exactly this.

138
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,780
But before I say anything
else,

139
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,190
I want to be straight with
you.

140
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,630
You've already had
something work fast.

141
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:40,490
The ice.

142
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,490
The first week of a new
pill.

143
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:44,140
The good day after a
session.

144
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,600
Then it wore off.

145
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:48,120
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

146
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,120
Fast relief isn't relief.

147
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,570
It's a preview.

148
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,710
So I'm not going to tell

149
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:53,990
you this works fast.

150
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:54,940
It doesn't.

151
00:03:55,090 --> 00:03:56,970
But if you're willing to
be patient,

152
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:58,060
and to look at what's
going

153
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,660
on around your new knee

154
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:01,010
instead of inside it,

155
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:02,450
there is a real reason

156
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,640
it still hurts.

157
00:04:03,770 --> 00:04:05,530
And something you can do
about it.

158
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:07,710
Let me explain what he
said,

159
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:08,810
because this is what
changed

160
00:04:08,810 --> 00:04:09,900
everything for me.

161
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,750
He started with the
basics.

162
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:13,310
A knee replacement takes
out

163
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,890
the worn joint surfaces

164
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:16,850
and puts in metal and
plastic.

165
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,930
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

166
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:20,630
you had before the
operation.

167
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,300
That part I already knew.

168
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,020
But then he explained
something

169
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:25,360
nobody had ever told me.

170
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:25,950
He said,

171
00:04:25,950 --> 00:04:27,470
think about a swollen foot

172
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:28,780
inside a shoe.

173
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:30,380
The shoe didn't shrink.

174
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:32,590
Your foot is taking up
more room,

175
00:04:32,590 --> 00:04:34,340
so everything feels
cramped

176
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:36,020
and tight and squeezed.

177
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:37,510
Your new knee sits

178
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,940
in a limited space with
living

179
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:40,630
tissue packed all around
it.

180
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,620
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

181
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,210
had to work through that
tissue.

182
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:47,000
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

183
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:48,660
At first that's normal.

184
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,390
But in some people that
swelling can

185
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,960
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

186
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:54,820
And swollen tissue takes
up more

187
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,500
room than calm tissue
does.

188
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:58,050
So when you bend,

189
00:04:58,050 --> 00:04:59,710
that tissue gets
compressed.

190
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:01,000
When you straighten,

191
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,100
it gets pulled tight.

192
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:02,780
That's the band.

193
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:04,940
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

194
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:06,600
And you start being the
one

195
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,320
who tells the young guy,

196
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:09,350
you take the kicker.

197
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:10,640
I'll do the trim.

198
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:12,380
And that's exactly why so
much

199
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:14,480
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

200
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,870
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

201
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:17,880
around the knee.

202
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,170
Worth doing,

203
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:20,210
and I'd done it.

204
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,030
It does nothing about
tissue

205
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,190
taking up room.

206
00:05:23,290 --> 00:05:25,720
A kneepad only cushions
the outside.

207
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,120
A nerve block quiets

208
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,530
the nerve carrying the
signal.

209
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:30,480
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

210
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,300
But when that irritated
tissue

211
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,730
finally calms down,

212
00:05:33,730 --> 00:05:35,030
it holds less fluid,

213
00:05:35,030 --> 00:05:36,410
and it takes up less room.

214
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:38,100
Less room taken up means

215
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,980
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

216
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:41,850
That's what takes the
pressure off.

217
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,660
After two years of this,

218
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:45,220
it finally made sense.

219
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,520
The problem was never the
new knee.

220
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,530
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

221
00:05:49,690 --> 00:05:51,280
He calls it the squeeze.

222
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:53,690
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

223
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,110
I'd bought knee sleeves,

224
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:57,200
compression braces,
creams,

225
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,430
every kneepad the supply
house sells,

226
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,310
half of Amazon really,

227
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,320
and all any of it gave

228
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,370
me was an hour.

229
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,480
I even looked at going

230
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,370
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

231
00:06:06,530 --> 00:06:08,010
But at $200 a session

232
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:09,910
with nothing covered by
insurance,

233
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:11,050
that was a quick no.

234
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:12,980
Then one night I went

235
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,230
back to that knee
replacement

236
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,740
group and actually read
it.

237
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:17,360
Thousands of people,

238
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,180
years out from surgery,

239
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:21,740
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

240
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:23,250
nobody could explain.

241
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,310
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

242
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:27,100
the same thing kept coming
up.

243
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,620
This one device,

244
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,240
and people saying it was
the first

245
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,700
thing that made a
difference.

246
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,920
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

247
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,370
alright, here it comes,

248
00:06:35,370 --> 00:06:36,780
he's selling me something,

249
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:39,030
let me shut that down
right now.

250
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,340
I'm only here because I

251
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:42,010
made myself a promise

252
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:43,330
at 2:30 in the morning

253
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:44,680
that if I ever found

254
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,880
something that helped,

255
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:46,830
I'd say so.

256
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:49,080
It's called the KenRelief
Red

257
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,480
Light Therapy Wrap.

258
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:53,190
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

259
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,070
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

260
00:06:55,070 --> 00:06:57,070
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

261
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,590
But I went to their
website anyway,

262
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:00,560
just to see what all

263
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,720
the fuss was about.

264
00:07:02,030 --> 00:07:04,100
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

265
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:06,490
charge $200 a session for,

266
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:09,230
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

267
00:07:09,230 --> 00:07:10,300
in a wrap you plug

268
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,590
into the wall at home.

269
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,490
Two hundred and forty
lights.

270
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,480
Red at 660 nanometers

271
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:18,240
and near-infrared at 850,

272
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,460
run together

273
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:20,790
for the strongest effect.

274
00:07:21,050 --> 00:07:22,420
Four strength levels.

275
00:07:22,570 --> 00:07:24,420
A five to thirty minute
timer.

276
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,860
Then I saw the guarantee.

277
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:27,370
Ninety days.

278
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:30,110
Results or your money
back,

279
00:07:30,110 --> 00:07:32,560
no questions, no store
credit,

280
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,590
and you don't even send it
back.

281
00:07:34,630 --> 00:07:37,210
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

282
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,850
days to change my mind.

283
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:40,520
There wasn't much to lose,

284
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,470
so I ordered it.

285
00:07:41,510 --> 00:07:42,940
Two of them, actually.

286
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:45,190
Only the right knee was
replaced,

287
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:47,400
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

288
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,340
and I'd done it for two
years.

289
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,270
On every job since,

290
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:53,420
the left one was carrying
the difference.

291
00:07:53,650 --> 00:07:54,480
When it came,

292
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,970
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

293
00:07:56,970 --> 00:07:58,280
because I'd been let down
too

294
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,800
many times to get excited.

295
00:07:59,990 --> 00:08:01,410
What I felt was warmth.

296
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,210
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

297
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,040
More like it was coming
from inside

298
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,710
the knee and spreading
around it.

299
00:08:07,030 --> 00:08:07,940
And that was it.

300
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:09,930
That was the whole
experience.

301
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,620
When I took it off,

302
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,920
I'll be honest,

303
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,030
nothing dramatic had
happened.

304
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,760
And after what that video
said,

305
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:19,090
that's exactly what I
expected.

306
00:08:19,370 --> 00:08:20,480
What was different

307
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,390
was that for the first

308
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,790
time in two years

309
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:24,680
I'd done something for my
knee

310
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,730
instead of to it.

311
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,310
Twenty minutes,

312
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,420
in my own chair.

313
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:30,690
No drive, no copay.

314
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:32,090
They say twenty minutes.

315
00:08:32,130 --> 00:08:33,090
I did thirty,

316
00:08:33,090 --> 00:08:34,150
twice a day,

317
00:08:34,150 --> 00:08:35,980
lowest setting that first
week.

318
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,410
Once before work, once
after.

319
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:39,710
The first week,

320
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:40,610
I couldn't have told

321
00:08:40,610 --> 00:08:42,360
you if anything was
happening.

322
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,490
I tried not to get

323
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:44,440
my hopes up.

324
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,420
I'd had things help

325
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:46,800
for a week and then stop.

326
00:08:46,950 --> 00:08:48,330
But somewhere in the
second week

327
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:49,410
I noticed I'd come down

328
00:08:49,410 --> 00:08:51,200
the stairs without holding
the rail.

329
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:52,710
I hadn't decided to.

330
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:54,160
I just did it, then
stopped

331
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:56,170
halfway down because I
realized.

332
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,460
By the end of the fourth

333
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,450
week I'd slept through

334
00:08:58,450 --> 00:09:00,510
the night four times
running.

335
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:01,680
I stood at the counter

336
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,470
and finished making dinner

337
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:05,130
without looking for the
stool.

338
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:06,820
None of that is dramatic.

339
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,720
All of it was gone

340
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,750
for two years.

341
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:10,530
A few weeks later my wife
asked

342
00:09:10,530 --> 00:09:11,390
if I wanted to walk

343
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:13,030
the long way around the
block.

344
00:09:13,270 --> 00:09:14,200
And for the first time

345
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:14,880
in two years,

346
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:15,970
I said yes.

347
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,730
I wanted to understand
why,

348
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:19,140
so I read the whole thing.

349
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:21,030
It comes down to four
steps.

350
00:09:21,070 --> 00:09:21,720
One.

351
00:09:22,030 --> 00:09:23,900
The tissue around a new
knee can

352
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:26,670
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

353
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:27,850
Two.

354
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,080
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

355
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:30,920
so it takes up more

356
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,020
room than it should.

357
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:32,830
Three.

358
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:34,320
There's only so much room
in there.

359
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,770
Bending compresses it.

360
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:37,150
Straightening pulls it
tight.

361
00:09:37,190 --> 00:09:38,460
That's the squeeze.

362
00:09:38,690 --> 00:09:39,430
Four.

363
00:09:39,910 --> 00:09:41,370
Red and near-infrared
light have been

364
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:43,310
studied for calming that
inflammation,

365
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:44,570
so the swelling and the
pressure

366
00:09:44,570 --> 00:09:45,710
can come down with it.

367
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,360
In a randomized trial,

368
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:49,400
patients given light
therapy

369
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:52,000
after a knee replacement
had less pain,

370
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,130
less swelling

371
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:54,540
and better early movement
than

372
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:55,530
those who weren't.

373
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:58,480
A 2025 review said the
same,

374
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,800
and was clear the evidence

375
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,810
is still limited.

376
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:02,360
I probably sound like a
broken

377
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,570
record to my crew.

378
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:06,100
But after two years of
doing everything

379
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,620
I was told and getting
nowhere,

380
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:09,910
you have no idea what it's

381
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:11,440
like to sleep through the
night,

382
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,790
say yes to the walk,

383
00:10:12,790 --> 00:10:14,230
and get my life back.

384
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,600
So take it from me.

385
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:17,420
Don't spend another year
waiting

386
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,420
for it to settle.

387
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,590
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

388
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:22,630
More than ten thousand
people

389
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,630
with pain after a knee
replacement

390
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:26,360
have already tried this.

391
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,620
Some had it worse than I
did.

392
